# The lexicon blobs are byte-exact data, not text.
#
# Git's autocrlf rewrote them to CRLF on Windows checkout, which appended a
# stray \r to every line. SortedBlobLexicon compares raw UTF-8 bytes, so every
# lookup then missed: CI failed on Windows while passing on Linux, and passed
# locally because the files had been *written* by the build script rather than
# checked out. Marking them binary stops the translation at the source.
packages/omniocr/src/omniocr/data/lexicons/*.txt -text

# Ground-truth transcriptions are compared byte-for-byte against OCR output by
# the CER gate, so they must not be translated either.
tests/corpus/*.txt -text
